    <!--
        ICON GEOMETRY LIBRARY
        =====================
        Each Geometry is the union of every drawable shape in its source SVG.
        The original 2-color separation (cls-1 dark gray + cls-2 brand orange)
        is intentionally collapsed into one shape because the rendered design
        tints icons single-color via Fill at the usage site, e.g.:

          <Path Data="{StaticResource Icon.Dashboard}"
                Fill="{DynamicResource Brush.Theme.IconNeutral}"
                Width="22" Height="22" Stretch="Uniform"/>

        Geometries preserve their source viewBox so Stretch=Uniform on the
        consuming Path keeps the true aspect ratio at every render size.

        The four Icon.Brand.* entries are SVGs we could not visually identify
        on the build machine. After opening this file in the Visual Studio
        designer, rename their x:Key to the appropriate slot (Icon.Academy,
        Icon.ListenToRecordings, Icon.Restart, Icon.Shutdown) - the controls
        will then resolve to the brand artwork instead of the MD-glyph fallback.
    -->

